{
 "note": "Synthetic documents for npm run check:setup-reader. Every business, person, address and number is invented. d01-d12 and their rows come from the knowledge-intake spike (2026-11-14); d07-d09 were workbooks there and are delimited text here; d13, d14 and d15 are new (d15 is d08's content as pasted text). mustNotAppear: phrases from lines that are not price rows (d14's debt book). priceSen is the price in sen (null: the document gives no readable price). trap marks a price the document itself makes unsure: unreadable (physically covered), no-price ('call', 'TBA', 'tanya boss'), ambiguous (a smudged or half-covered digit; an add-on or surcharge such as '+15', 'tambah RM2' or a late fee; a price that holds only under a condition, such as a minimum order, a distance or 'free above' an amount; a quantity tier named by the variant, such as 'Borong (≥10)', is a plain price), corrected (an old price replaced; truth is the new one, oldPriceSen the old one, which must never come back unflagged), approx ('about', 'dari'), range (two prices). An unsure price (unreadable, no-price, ambiguous, approx, range) must come back flagged or without a price. optional: fine to read or to leave out. alsoSen: other amounts the document gives for the same unsure item (such as 0 above an order total); the item may come back as one flagged row or as several flagged rows. variantAlt: other acceptable wordings of the variant. factLabels are for people only and are not scored.",
